  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 200 PM EDT Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Heat and humidity will persist through the \nweekend and into early next week. Low, but daily chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms continue through Sunday, mainly along \nand north of a line from Richmond to Salisbury.\n\nBermuda high pressure surface-aloft prevails off the Southeast \ncoast this afternoon. Meanwhile, a trough is digging into the \nOhio Valley. Showers/tstms are developing along the Blue Ridge \nthis afternoon. SBCAPE is ~3000J/kg locally. However, shear is \nweak and there is a mid-level cap, so most of this activity \nshould remain N of the local area through the afternoon and \nevening. However, any tstm will be capable of producing some \nlocally stronger wind gusts along the northern tier of the area \nwith DCAPE at or above 800 J/kg. Through the weekend the weather\npattern will remain quite similar with daily chances of showers\nand thunderstorms along the lee trough and high terrain and sea\nbreeze, but most area should be dry. In addition to the showers\nand tstms, the heat and humidity will persist with temps \nranging in the low to middle 90s and Heat Indices between the \nupper 90s and low 100s but again remaining shy of the 105F Heat \nAdvisory criteria.\n\nBy early next week ensembles hint on a more zonal pattern \nacross the area with the strongest flow remaining north of the \narea. While at the surface high pressure continues to thrive off\nthe coast continuing to usher in heat and moisture. During the \nearly to mid- week stretch the chances of showers and tstms \npersist (mainly N) with the best chance possibly Wednesday as a \nstronger cold front tries to move into the area. Outside of the \ndaily chances of showers/tstms, temperatures are expected to \nrise above normal with temperatures possibly reaching into the \nlower 90s. With dew points struggling to mix through the day as \nthe high is offshore they will remain the low to middle 70s \nagain allowing Heat Indices to be in the low 100s. Will note \nthere is a possibility that some places could reach Heat \nAdvisory criteria Tues and Wed but confidence at this time \nremains low.",
